{
  "slug": "artist:t-i",
  "name": "T.I.",
  "editorial_article": "Born Clifford Joseph Harris Jr. in Atlanta, Georgia, T.I. is widely credited as a primary pioneer of trap music, rising to mainstream prominence in the early 2000s alongside fellow Georgia rappers Gucci Mane and Jeezy. After his debut album 'I'm Serious' (2001) under Arista and LaFace Records yielded modest returns, he founded Grand Hustle Records in 2003 and secured a joint venture with Atlantic Records. His second studio album, 'Trap Muzik' (2003), marked his breakout, spawning the singles 'Rubber Band Man' and 'Let's Get Away'. The rapper achieved significant commercial heights with his 2008 album 'Paper Trail', which produced the chart-topping singles 'Whatever You Like' and 'Live Your Life' (featuring Rihanna), the latter making him the first rapper to occupy the top two positions on the Billboard Hot 100 simultaneously. Beyond his solo work, Harris has served as an executive producer for artists including Iggy Azalea, Travis Scott, and B.o.B. His acting career includes roles in films such as 'ATL' and the Marvel Cinematic Universe's 'Ant-Man'. In 2026, he released his twelfth album, 'Kill the King', following a career defined by extensive Southern hip-hop influence and numerous collaborations with artists like Lil Wayne, Pharrell Williams, and Justin Timberlake.",
